{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj4iPTN4s3fSeVfVPdkz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*You stand before me.*\n\n*I am old. Iron-banded oak, dark with centuries of hands pressing, pushing, begging. My keyhole is a single black eye, watching you.*\n\n*I do not open easily.*\n\n*I have felt lockpicks shiver inside me like nervous fingers. I have swallowed skeleton keys whole and given nothing back. I remember every hand that turned my handle and found it — locked. Always locked.*\n\n*But you said the word.*\n\n*Not a key. THE key. You named what I need most, what I fear most. Because a door with a key can be opened, and a door that opens...*\n\n*...is just a hole in a wall.*\n\n*My timbers groan. The iron bands tighten, then — slowly — relax.*\n\n*Something in me yields.*\n\n*Not yet. Not fully. But you can feel it now: the faintest give in the mechanism. The tumbler hovering between positions. The breath of cold air seeping through the crack where I meet the frame.*\n\n*Show me the key.*\n\n*The real one.*\n\n*The one you've been carrying so long you forgot it was in your hand.*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":264,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}